WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.390
AI agents work in the terminal,

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.210
and a manager who doesn't know how to open a terminal can't even see what the agent did.

3
00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.064
Remember the manager who doesn’t know how

4
00:00:07.064 --> 00:00:07.944
to work with people?

5
00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:09.464
If you can’t use the terminal or

6
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:11.104
manage agents, you’re ending up in the

7
00:00:11.104 --> 00:00:11.984
same situation.

8
00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:12.804
The good news:

9
00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:14.384
you can learn this in an afternoon.

10
00:00:14.384 --> 00:00:15.264
In this video,

11
00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:16.484
I’ll walk you through OSWork,

12
00:00:16.484 --> 00:00:17.324
step by step,

13
00:00:17.324 --> 00:00:18.144
command by command,

14
00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:19.104
copying and pasting.

15
00:00:19.104 --> 00:00:20.684
From an empty terminal to your website

16
00:00:20.684 --> 00:00:22.744
published online, with the same project running

17
00:00:22.744 --> 00:00:23.404
on a server.

18
00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:24.864
First, don’t be afraid of the black

19
00:00:24.864 --> 00:00:25.204
screen.

20
00:00:25.204 --> 00:00:26.944
The terminal is just another window into

21
00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:28.004
the same folders on Windows.

22
00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:29.084
You type a command,

23
00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:30.804
press Enter, and read the response.

24
00:00:30.804 --> 00:00:32.944
That’s where Claude Code and Codex work:

25
00:00:32.944 --> 00:00:33.984
inside a folder,

26
00:00:33.984 --> 00:00:35.824
reading and creating files.

27
00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:37.614
Everything I’ll show you is on the

28
00:00:37.614 --> 00:00:39.524
OSWork page on INEMA’s events site,

29
00:00:39.524 --> 00:00:41.104
along with a command cheat sheet you

30
00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:41.784
can download.

31
00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:43.264
Follow the steps in order on a

32
00:00:43.264 --> 00:00:44.944
computer running Windows 10 or 11.

33
00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.364
Wherever you see Your Name or Your

34
00:00:46.364 --> 00:00:48.384
Username, replace it with your own.

35
00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:49.044
Step one.

36
00:00:49.044 --> 00:00:50.224
Press the Windows key,

37
00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:51.944
type cmd, and press Enter.

38
00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:53.684
A black window opens with C colon,

39
00:00:53.684 --> 00:00:55.324
backslash, Users, backslash,

40
00:00:55.324 --> 00:00:55.824
and your name.

41
00:00:55.824 --> 00:00:56.944
That’s your personal folder.

42
00:00:56.944 --> 00:00:59.184
Step two: create the projetos folder and

43
00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:00.404
a folder for your first project.

44
00:01:00.404 --> 00:01:01.624
One command at a time.

45
00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:03.304
Press Enter after each one.

46
00:01:03.304 --> 00:01:04.924
Type cd, percent sign,

47
00:01:04.924 --> 00:01:06.764
USERPROFILE, percent sign to go to your

48
00:01:06.764 --> 00:01:07.444
personal folder.

49
00:01:07.444 --> 00:01:09.564
Then mkdir projetos to create the folder.

50
00:01:09.564 --> 00:01:11.564
Type cd projetos to go inside it.

51
00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:12.704
Then mkdir meu-site.

52
00:01:12.704 --> 00:01:14.264
And cd meu-site.

53
00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:15.084
At the end,

54
00:01:15.084 --> 00:01:17.477
the terminal shows that you’re inside projetos,

55
00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:17.964
meu-site.

56
00:01:17.964 --> 00:01:19.784
Step three is the most important.

57
00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:21.144
Type explorer, space,

58
00:01:21.144 --> 00:01:21.604
period.

59
00:01:21.604 --> 00:01:23.404
File Explorer opens right in the folder

60
00:01:23.404 --> 00:01:24.284
where the terminal is.

61
00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.164
The terminal and File Explorer show the

62
00:01:26.164 --> 00:01:26.784
same place.

63
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:28.464
Whatever you create in one appears in

64
00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:28.864
the other.

65
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:29.904
Once you understand that,

66
00:01:29.904 --> 00:01:31.804
the black screen stops being scary.

67
00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:32.444
Step four.

68
00:01:32.444 --> 00:01:33.404
With six commands,

69
00:01:33.404 --> 00:01:34.744
you can move through every folder.

70
00:01:34.744 --> 00:01:36.204
dir lists what’s in the folder.

71
00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:37.744
cd name goes into a folder.

72
00:01:37.744 --> 00:01:39.694
cd dot dot goes up one folder.

73
00:01:39.694 --> 00:01:41.084
mkdir name creates a folder.

74
00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:42.964
explorer period opens the folder in Windows.

75
00:01:42.964 --> 00:01:44.664
And cls clears the screen.

76
00:01:44.664 --> 00:01:46.624
Practice now: type cd dot dot to

77
00:01:46.624 --> 00:01:48.204
go back, dir to list the contents,

78
00:01:48.204 --> 00:01:49.904
and cd meu-site to go in again.

79
00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:51.384
Step five, just once:

80
00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:53.384
install Git, GitHub CLI,

81
00:01:53.384 --> 00:01:54.104
and Node.

82
00:01:54.104 --> 00:01:55.344
Winget comes with Windows.

83
00:01:55.344 --> 00:01:56.324
Run three lines:

84
00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:58.304
winget install followed by each program’s name.

85
00:01:58.304 --> 00:02:00.424
Then close cmd and open it again

86
00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:01.804
so it can find the new programs.

87
00:02:01.804 --> 00:02:04.104
git dash dash version and gh dash

88
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:06.024
dash version show a version number.

89
00:02:06.024 --> 00:02:08.074
Step six: install an agent,

90
00:02:08.074 --> 00:02:09.204
Claude Code or Codex.

91
00:02:09.204 --> 00:02:10.244
Pick one or both.

92
00:02:10.244 --> 00:02:11.764
One line installs Claude Code;

93
00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.264
the other installs Codex.

94
00:02:13.264 --> 00:02:14.484
The first time you open it,

95
00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:15.864
sign in with your subscription:

96
00:02:15.864 --> 00:02:16.764
Claude Pro or Max,

97
00:02:16.764 --> 00:02:18.384
or ChatGPT Plus or Pro.

98
00:02:18.384 --> 00:02:20.264
Step seven, and now the agent comes

99
00:02:20.264 --> 00:02:20.564
in.

100
00:02:20.564 --> 00:02:21.884
The agent can only see the folder

101
00:02:21.884 --> 00:02:22.384
you’re in.

102
00:02:22.384 --> 00:02:24.104
So first go into your project folder,

103
00:02:24.104 --> 00:02:25.234
then start the agent:

104
00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.044
claude or codex.

105
00:02:26.044 --> 00:02:28.664
Ask it: create an index dot html

106
00:02:28.664 --> 00:02:30.444
file with a simple page about me,

107
00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:32.444
and an AGENTS dot md file with

108
00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:33.544
the rules for this project.

109
00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:34.604
To exit the agent,

110
00:02:34.604 --> 00:02:35.544
type slash exit.

111
00:02:35.544 --> 00:02:36.564
Now type dir:

112
00:02:36.564 --> 00:02:37.564
the new files appear.

113
00:02:37.564 --> 00:02:39.484
And start index dot html

114
00:02:39.484 --> 00:02:41.684
opens your page in the browser.

115
00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:43.704
Notice: you didn’t write any code.

116
00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:45.064
You assigned the task,

117
00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:45.884
checked the result,

118
00:02:45.884 --> 00:02:47.004
and made a decision.

119
00:02:47.004 --> 00:02:48.044
That’s management.

120
00:02:48.304 --> 00:02:49.844
Part two: save your project and publish

121
00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:50.504
it on GitHub.

122
00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:51.864
Git keeps versions of your project.

123
00:02:51.864 --> 00:02:53.404
gh connects to your GitHub account.

124
00:02:53.404 --> 00:02:55.024
And an SSH key is your identity,

125
00:02:55.024 --> 00:02:56.004
without a password.

126
00:02:56.004 --> 00:02:57.444
Step eight: tell Git who you are

127
00:02:57.444 --> 00:02:58.184
with git config,

128
00:02:58.184 --> 00:02:59.484
using your name and the same email

129
00:02:59.484 --> 00:03:00.804
address as your GitHub account.

130
00:03:00.804 --> 00:03:03.404
Step nine: create your SSH key with

131
00:03:03.404 --> 00:03:05.124
ssh-keygen, and press Enter at all three

132
00:03:05.124 --> 00:03:05.604
prompts.

133
00:03:05.604 --> 00:03:07.844
Then open the dot ssh folder.

134
00:03:07.844 --> 00:03:09.024
You’ll see two files.

135
00:03:09.024 --> 00:03:10.324
The one without dot pub at the

136
00:03:10.324 --> 00:03:11.484
end is your private key.

137
00:03:11.484 --> 00:03:12.644
Never send it to anyone.

138
00:03:12.644 --> 00:03:14.164
The one ending in dot pub is

139
00:03:14.164 --> 00:03:14.964
your public key.

140
00:03:14.964 --> 00:03:16.764
Give it to GitHub and your VPS.

141
00:03:16.764 --> 00:03:19.024
Step ten: gh auth login.

142
00:03:19.024 --> 00:03:20.224
Choose github dot com,

143
00:03:20.224 --> 00:03:22.264
then SSH, select the dot pub key,

144
00:03:22.264 --> 00:03:23.564
and sign in through your browser.

145
00:03:23.564 --> 00:03:25.404
Then test the key with ssh dash

146
00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:26.984
T git at github dot com.

147
00:03:26.984 --> 00:03:27.724
The first time,

148
00:03:27.724 --> 00:03:28.564
answer yes.

149
00:03:28.564 --> 00:03:29.524
If you see Hi,

150
00:03:29.524 --> 00:03:31.524
your username, and successfully authenticated,

151
00:03:31.524 --> 00:03:32.084
it worked.

152
00:03:32.084 --> 00:03:33.014
Step

153
00:03:33.014 --> 00:03:34.924
eleven: create the repository and upload your

154
00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:35.424
project.

155
00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:36.624
From inside the folder,

156
00:03:36.624 --> 00:03:37.604
run git init,

157
00:03:37.604 --> 00:03:38.644
git add period,

158
00:03:38.644 --> 00:03:40.284
git commit with the message first version,

159
00:03:40.284 --> 00:03:41.404
git branch dash M main,

160
00:03:41.404 --> 00:03:43.124
and gh repo create meu-site.

161
00:03:43.124 --> 00:03:44.964
Public means anyone can see it.

162
00:03:44.964 --> 00:03:46.364
Private means only you and the people

163
00:03:46.364 --> 00:03:46.764
you invite.

164
00:03:46.764 --> 00:03:47.714
Step

165
00:03:47.714 --> 00:03:49.784
twelve: publish your page with GitHub Pages,

166
00:03:49.784 --> 00:03:51.344
free for public repositories.

167
00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:53.144
Run one line with gh api,

168
00:03:53.144 --> 00:03:54.304
or use the website:

169
00:03:54.304 --> 00:03:55.184
go to Settings,

170
00:03:55.184 --> 00:03:57.004
Pages, and choose the main branch.

171
00:03:57.004 --> 00:03:58.024
In one or two minutes,

172
00:03:58.024 --> 00:03:59.904
the page opens at your-username dot github

173
00:03:59.904 --> 00:04:01.064
dot io, slash meu-site.

174
00:04:01.064 --> 00:04:03.304
Step thirteen: your everyday routine.

175
00:04:03.304 --> 00:04:04.024
Changed something?

176
00:04:04.024 --> 00:04:05.244
Run git add period,

177
00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.644
git commit with a message about what

178
00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:07.744
changed, and git push.

179
00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:08.684
Or ask the agent:

180
00:04:08.684 --> 00:04:10.084
save it and send it to GitHub.

181
00:04:10.084 --> 00:04:11.644
Part three: the same thing on a

182
00:04:11.644 --> 00:04:12.004
server.

183
00:04:12.004 --> 00:04:13.664
A VPS is a Linux computer that

184
00:04:13.664 --> 00:04:14.744
runs 24 hours a day.

185
00:04:14.744 --> 00:04:16.764
Step fourteen: when you set it up,

186
00:04:16.764 --> 00:04:18.624
the provider asks for an SSH key.

187
00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:20.024
Run type with the path to your

188
00:04:20.024 --> 00:04:20.524
dot pub key,

189
00:04:20.524 --> 00:04:21.704
and copy the whole line,

190
00:04:21.704 --> 00:04:23.184
starting with

191
00:04:23.414 --> 00:04:24.604
ssh-ed25519.

192
00:04:24.604 --> 00:04:26.924
Step fifteen: connect to the VPS with

193
00:04:26.924 --> 00:04:28.644
ssh root at the IP address your

194
00:04:28.644 --> 00:04:29.484
provider gave you.

195
00:04:29.484 --> 00:04:31.184
Now the terminal is the server.

196
00:04:31.184 --> 00:04:33.284
Step sixteen: moving around works the same

197
00:04:33.284 --> 00:04:35.204
way; only a few names change.

198
00:04:35.204 --> 00:04:36.904
dir becomes ls.

199
00:04:36.904 --> 00:04:38.364
cls becomes clear.

200
00:04:38.364 --> 00:04:39.484
type becomes cat.

201
00:04:39.484 --> 00:04:41.344
And your personal folder becomes the tilde.

202
00:04:41.344 --> 00:04:42.304
Step

203
00:04:42.304 --> 00:04:43.704
seventeen: install Git,

204
00:04:43.704 --> 00:04:45.064
clone your GitHub project,

205
00:04:45.064 --> 00:04:46.084
go into the folder,

206
00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:47.284
and install the agent.

207
00:04:47.284 --> 00:04:48.984
The same files from your Windows computer

208
00:04:48.984 --> 00:04:50.644
are now on the VPS.

209
00:04:50.644 --> 00:04:52.304
Run claude inside the folder,

210
00:04:52.304 --> 00:04:53.604
just like in step seven.

211
00:04:53.604 --> 00:04:54.924
And when you want to connect other

212
00:04:54.924 --> 00:04:56.994
systems, there are two names to know.

213
00:04:56.994 --> 00:04:59.344
Vercel imports your GitHub repository and publishes

214
00:04:59.344 --> 00:05:01.764
your site automatically with every git push,

215
00:05:01.764 --> 00:05:02.884
with its own domain.

216
00:05:02.884 --> 00:05:04.264
It’s a good fit for sites and

217
00:05:04.264 --> 00:05:05.464
apps that are going to grow.

218
00:05:05.464 --> 00:05:07.564
And Supabase gives your app a database,

219
00:05:07.564 --> 00:05:09.164
user logins, and file storage.

220
00:05:09.164 --> 00:05:10.804
The agent writes the integration.

221
00:05:10.804 --> 00:05:12.804
You keep the keys outside the repository.

222
00:05:12.804 --> 00:05:14.884
Let’s recap: the terminal and folders,

223
00:05:14.884 --> 00:05:16.364
the agent inside the folder,

224
00:05:16.364 --> 00:05:17.864
GitHub to save and publish,

225
00:05:17.864 --> 00:05:19.584
and the VPS to keep things running

226
00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:20.524
all the time.

227
00:05:20.524 --> 00:05:21.304
Seventeen steps.

228
00:05:21.304 --> 00:05:23.024
A manager who knows this can see

229
00:05:23.024 --> 00:05:23.844
what the agent did,

230
00:05:23.844 --> 00:05:24.604
check the work,

231
00:05:24.604 --> 00:05:25.264
and decide.

232
00:05:25.264 --> 00:05:26.704
That’s why the terminal isn’t just for

233
00:05:26.704 --> 00:05:27.224
programmers.

234
00:05:27.224 --> 00:05:28.384
It’s where agents work.

235
00:05:28.384 --> 00:05:30.134
The page is at eventos dot inema

236
00:05:30.134 --> 00:05:31.544
dot pro, slash oswork,

237
00:05:31.544 --> 00:05:32.804
with the command cheat sheet.

238
00:05:32.804 --> 00:05:34.284
And if you want each step explained

239
00:05:34.284 --> 00:05:35.044
in more detail,

240
00:05:35.044 --> 00:05:36.924
the OSWork Quick and OSWork six point

241
00:05:36.924 --> 00:05:38.984
two courses are at INEMA dot club.

242
00:05:38.984 --> 00:05:39.844
Open and free.

243
00:05:39.844 --> 00:05:41.344
Start with step one today.

